---
# LLVM's defaults already are this project's house style: 2-space indent, 80
# columns, braces attached, `Type &name`, and short if-bodies kept on their own
# line. Adopting the base style wholesale rather than hand-listing it keeps this
# file short and leaves fewer settings to drift.
BasedOnStyle: LLVM

# Include order is hand-maintained. JuceHeader.h has to come first in the files
# that use it, and sorting moves it.
SortIncludes: false

# Comments here carry the reasoning -- protocol citations, invariants, the
# occasional measured number -- and they are wrapped by hand so the emphasis
# falls where it was meant to. Reflowing them produces things like a citation
# broken after "tagged form," and gains nothing. The formatter owns the code;
# the prose is the author's.
ReflowComments: false
...
